A towering babel-like structure made of interconnected puzzle pieces, each piece carved from different materials—polished steel, weathered wood, translucent glass, rough stone—all attempting to lock together but visibly misaligned at their edges. The structure spirals upward against a dramatic stormy sky, with some pieces floating nearby, trying to find their place. Golden light breaks through dark clouds, illuminating the gaps and mismatches between the puzzle sections. The scene conveys both ambition and frustration, order attempting to emerge from incompatibility. Style: Vincent van Gogh—bold swirling brushstrokes in the sky, thick impasto texture on the puzzle pieces, vivid contrasting colors of deep blues, bright yellows, and burnt oranges, emotional intensity radiating from every element.
